{title: Nearer, My God, to Thee}
{key: G}
{tempo: 76}
{time: 6/4}
{meta: author Sarah Fuller Flower Adams}
{meta: author Lowell Mason}
{meta: year 1841}
{meta: died 1848}
{meta: died 1872}
{meta: source WorshipCommons, https://worshipcommons.org/songs/ggzFvLEr9mK}
{copyright: Public domain}

Verse 1
[G]Nearer, my [D]God, to [G]thee, [C]nearer to [D]thee!
[G]E'en though it [D]be a [Em]cross that [C]raiseth [D]me,
[G]still all my [D]song shall [G]be: nearer, my [C]God, to thee,
[G]nearer, my [C]God, to [D]thee, [G]nearer to [D]thee!

Verse 2
Though like the wanderer, the sun gone down,
Darkness be over me, my rest a stone,
Yet in my dreams I'd be nearer, my God, to Thee,
Nearer, my God, to Thee, nearer to Thee!
